# Tracer: one known left edge supplies the middle point of real-order transitivity.
# Before:
# forall x R:
#     x <= 900
#     =>:
#         not x > 1070
# Former route: NegatedOrder plus specialized NumericUpperBoundWeakenLe.
# Now: write the positive intermediate explicitly; its proof uses one shared
# transitivity search and a checked numeric residual, with no numeric-bound scan.
forall x R:
    x <= 900
    =>:
        x <= 1070
        not x > 1070

forall a, b, c R:
    a <= b
    b <= c
    =>:
        a <= c

forall x R:
    x >= 1260
    =>:
        x >= 1250

forall x R:
    x < 900
    =>:
        x < 1070

forall x R:
    x > 1260
    =>:
        x > 1250

# Boundary: no reverse search, mixed-relation search, or second transitivity.
# The bare negative goal above now requires the explicit positive intermediate.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -lang en -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/atomic/by_builtin_rewrite/one_step_order_transitivity.lit
# Rejection controls: tests/unit/execute/registered_transitivity/tests.rs.
# Implementation: search_transitive_relation.rs and builtin rewrite dispatcher.
